---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Pricing | Podomy"
		description="Podomy software is free under AGPLv3. Startups pay $10,000 per year flat with unlimited nodes. Enterprise is priced per node. No SLAs, no support contracts."
	currentPath="/pricing/"
>
	<h1 class="page-title">Pricing</h1>
	<p class="body-p">
		Clear numbers. No sales maze.
	</p>

	<section class="content-section" style="margin-top: 0;">
		<p class="body-p">
			Podomy software is free to use under AGPLv3 when your application remains open source.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">For proprietary use</h2>
		</div>
		<ul class="bullet-list">
			<li><strong>Startups: $10,000/year flat.</strong> Unlimited nodes. Companies with less than $1M in annual revenue.</li>
			<li><strong>Enterprise:</strong> Companies with $1M+ in annual revenue. Priced per node.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="body-p">
			A node is one physical server or distinct cloud instance running the runtime.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Terms</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			Annual licenses cover production use of the software. We don't offer support contracts or SLAs. If you need hands-on help, <a href="/contact/" class="body-link">consulting</a> is available separately.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Try it first</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			One binary. Two nodes. Cut the network.
		</p>
		<p class="body-p">
			<a href="/docs/deployment/" class="body-link">Deployment guide</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<p class="body-p">
		<a href="/contact/" class="body-link">Contact engineering</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
